      "strategy": "incremental_by_identity via the governed_merge custom materialization: unique_key trade_number; frozen_columns (owning_account_number, placed_at, owning_account_effective_from, owning_customer_number, owning_customer_effective_from, first_seen_late, order_type) computed from each trade's first report and written only on insert; mutable_columns (status, executed_price, fees, commission, tax, quantity) computed from the latest I- or U-flagged raw.trade_cdc report and refreshed on match. placed_at (and the status used for first_seen_late) prefer the trade's earliest raw.trade_history row where one exists, else the earliest raw.trade_cdc row by report_order; owning_account_number and order_type are always the earliest raw.trade_cdc row's t_ca_id and t_tt_id (raw.trade_history carries no account or order-type field). first_seen_late compares the first-encountered report's status against order_type's own first lifecycle event in trade_code_meanings.status_order (PNDG for a limit order TLB/TLS, SBMT for a market order TMB/TMS), undefined (NULL) for an order_type outside those four codes. owning_account_effective_from/owning_customer_number resolved via as_of_event_time against governed.account at placed_at; owning_customer_effective_from resolved via as_of_event_time against governed.customer, for the customer named by that pinned account statement, at placed_at."
    }
